 "notes": "Solid black 'DD current' 95% CL bound from Fig. 2b (g_phigamma [eV^-1] vs m_phi), digitised from the embedded raster figure (g_DM_gamma_gen_mass_5th_proj_no_title.pdf) by tracing the lower boundary of the shaded excluded region; axis calibration from decade gridlines (x: 10^-14..10^-8 eV, y: 10^0..10^-40 eV^-1). The curve is extremely spiky (sensitivity lost at harmonics of the DD sequence); reported points are the lower envelope (per-bin minimum), i.e. the strongest bound locally. Conversion to Damour-Donoghue d_e: paper defines delta_alpha/alpha = g_phigamma*phi (Eq. 1-2), so d_e = g_phigamma/kappa with kappa = sqrt(4pi)/M_Pl = 2.906e-28 eV^-1. Paper assumes rho_DM = 3.1e-6 eV^4 = 0.40 GeV/cm^3 (local density near Sun). Generic-scalar scenario (independent couplings) chosen as main result; the paper also bounds g_phie (Fig 2a), relaxion mixing angle (Fig 2c) and a relaxion-star scenario (Fig 3, enhanced density) which are not reported here. Dashed 'DD projected' curve (projection) excluded.",
